From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cryolitia PukNgae <cryolitia.pukngae@linux.dev>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 20:37:42 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] media: iris: Use the measured decoder input rate for
 bandwidth

The decoder already tracks the rate at which source buffers arrive for
clock scaling, but the bandwidth lookup always uses 30 frames per
second. Use the observed decode rate for the bandwidth vote while
preserving the encoder default.

Calculate the rate from the number of inter-buffer intervals and their
elapsed time. At stream start the input rate is unknown, so start
conservatively until the first window of samples is available, as the
Qualcomm VIDC driver does for startup.

Codex compared the vendor and Linux source, checked the rate calculation
and built the modified objects. The combined change was tested on Piano
with 1080p60 and 4K60, and with 1080p playback switching between 30 and
60 frames per second, including a pause and resume.

Link: https://github.com/OnePlusOSS/android_kernel_modules_and_devicetree_oneplus_sm8750/blob/d50b305f7da9e14715a25120a4ac7b1a4b8b97c3/vendor/qcom/opensource/video-driver/driver/vidc/src/msm_vidc_power.c#L217-L250
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Cryolitia PukNgae <cryolitia.pukngae@linux.dev>
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_power.c | 2 +-
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vdec.c  | 9 +++++++--
 2 files changed, 8 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_power.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_power.c
index cceb31b80..94b9f5606 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_power.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_power.c
@@ -69,7 +69,7 @@ static int iris_vote_interconnects(struct iris_inst *inst)
 
 	vote_data->width = inp_f->fmt.pix_mp.width;
 	vote_data->height = inp_f->fmt.pix_mp.height;
-	vote_data->fps = DEFAULT_FPS;
+	vote_data->fps = inst->domain == DECODER ? inst->frame_rate : DEFAULT_FPS;
 
 	inst->power.icc_bw = iris_calc_bw(inst, vote_data);
 
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vdec.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vdec.c
index 9e228b704..282989249 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vdec.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vdec.c
@@ -3,6 +3,7 @@
  * Copyright (c) 2022-2024 Qualcomm Innovation Center, Inc. All rights reserved.
  */
 
+#include <linux/math64.h>
 #include <media/v4l2-event.h>
 #include <media/v4l2-mem2mem.h>
 
@@ -385,6 +386,7 @@ int iris_vdec_streamon_input(struct iris_inst *inst)
 		return ret;
 
 	inst->frame_counter = 0;
+	inst->frame_rate = MAXIMUM_FPS;
 
 	return iris_process_streamon_input(inst);
 }
@@ -455,8 +457,11 @@ int iris_vdec_qbuf(struct iris_inst *inst, struct vb2_v4l2_buffer *vbuf)
 		delta_ns = cur_buf_ns - inst->last_buf_ns;
 
 		if (delta_ns >= NSEC_PER_SEC) {
-			inst->frame_rate = clamp_t(u32, inst->frame_counter, DEFAULT_FPS,
-						   MAXIMUM_FPS);
+			/* Measure the intervals between the queued buffers. */
+			u64 frames = inst->frame_counter - 1;
+			u64 fps = DIV64_U64_ROUND_CLOSEST(frames * NSEC_PER_SEC, delta_ns);
+
+			inst->frame_rate = clamp_t(u32, fps, DEFAULT_FPS, MAXIMUM_FPS);
 			inst->frame_counter = 0;
 		}
 	}
-- 
